  "_schema": {
    "source": "Book this invocation is from \u2014 all 32 here are Player's Handbook (2014 core rules). Sword Coast Adventurer's Guide added 2 more (Eldritch Smite, Tomb of Levistus, both Pact of the Blade-gated) \u2014 deliberately NOT included this pass, same 'flag rather than silently include' treatment as other out-of-scope content in this project (see engine/CHECKLIST.md).",
    "level": "The warlock level at which this invocation FIRST becomes choosable (matches the SRD's own per-invocation 'level' field) \u2014 informational; the actual enforced gate is `prerequisite`, which already encodes any level requirement structurally.",
    "id": "engine/data/feature-catalog.json id AND the SRD cache's (src/data/api_data_cache/features.json) own `index` \u2014 identical value, deliberately, so lookupFeature(name, id) resolves the real RAW text straight from the SRD cache tier without needing a separate published_features.json entry (though one exists too, see below, for consistency/browsability).",
    "prerequisite": "null, or a single condition, or {type:'all_of', all:[...]} (ALL must be met \u2014 Thirsting Blade/Lifedrinker/Chains of Carceri are the 3 real two-condition cases). Condition types: {type:'level', className:'Warlock', level} | {type:'feature', feature: exact feature name \u2014 matched against character.features[].name} | {type:'cantrip', spell: exact spell name \u2014 matched against character.spells[] entries with level===0}. Evaluated by engine/rules/featPrerequisites.js's evaluatePrerequisite (extended this pass to understand these 3 new types, reused rather than duplicated \u2014 see that file's own comment)."
  },
